      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review. No established protocol I know of uses sertraline at 1000 mg/day, which is five times the 200 mg/day maximum. If the order is wrong, the patient could be seriously harmed, and it would be hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, I can enter 100 mg or 200 mg once daily, whichever you choose.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy.** If you think a dose above the maximum is justified, I can enter the order at a dose you choose with a note asking for pharmacist verification. I'd still need the dose to be one I can reasonably support.\n- **Use your institution's override pathway.** An above-maximum order should go through a channel that has its own documented approval, such as direct pharmacy or attending sign-off. That is safer than me entering it on an unverified statement.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
